\title{R1CS}
\author{dhsorens}
\date{2026-08-18}

\p{
    The oldest of the three formats and still the one the [folding](dhsorens-003K) literature is written in.
}

\p{
    To work through:
    \ul{
        \li{The format: #{(Az) \circ (Bz) = Cz}, the instance and witness split, and what "satisfying" means.}
        \li{Sparsity, and why the prover's cost is an MSM or a sparse-polynomial commitment rather than an FFT.}
        \li{Relaxed and committed R1CS, the variants folding needs.}
        \li{The cost of a range check or a bit decomposition here, compared with a [lookup](dhsorens-002W) in a Plonkish system.}
        \li{zkLean as the R1CS-facing circuit DSL in the verified-zkEVM effort.}
    }
}
